nd how fast it can move data. The math units are like a huge kitchen with hundreds of chefs. The memory is like the walk-in pantry and delivery trucks. If the chefs can chop 100,000 onions per second, but the pantry only lets out 10 onions per second, the kitchen is not slow because the chefs are lazy; it is slow because ingredients arrive too slowly.\n\nA GPU often has to read textures, colors, depth, and other data from memory before it can compute. If the data does not arrive", "top2": [[[1596, -0.003001839853823185], [22916, -6.394729137420654]], [[1144, -1.0609683158691041e-05], [513, -12.53760051727295]], [[4087, -0.5552769899368286], [310, -0.891790509223938]], [[1156, -0.004490069579333067], [310, -5.606105804443359]], [[579, -0.18762075901031494], [25, -1.9030578136444092]], [[1622, -0.00013030423724558204], [3296, -9.509488105773926]], [[25, -0.4216245412826538], [13, -1.1680881977081299]], [[10033, -0.3303848206996918], [79091, -1.6577240228652954]], [[310, -0.013947746716439724], [303, -4.292272090911865]], [[21520, -0.2214561402797699], [1496, -1.629661202430725]], [[1496, -0.008871330879628658], [32308, -4.734317779541016]], [[33541, -0.030051369220018387], [2812, -3.520453453063965]], [[5286, -0.00029693482792936265], [261, -8.249693870544434]], [[11, -0.4272087514400482], [303, -1.3307522535324097]], [[883, -0.07837659120559692], [3835, -3.258626699447632]], [[220, -4.172333774477011e-06], [19, -12.88672161102295]], [[19, -2.1815538275404833e-05], [20, -11.26680850982666]], [[15, -1.2993897144042421e-05], [18, -12.14680290222168]], [[15, -9.536747711536009e-07], [16, -14.912331581115723]], [[4105, -4.768382950715022e-06], [3069, -12.81103229522705]], [[11, -0.0041587878949940205], [13, -5.517138481140137]], [[3069, -1.3589951777248643e-05], [33488, -12.670190811157227]], [[21966, -0.6035425662994385], [13775, -0.8490259647369385]], [[6973, -0.5173245668411255], [628, -0.9301263689994812]], [[539, -4.0531240301788785e-06], [4779, -12.407365798950195]]